    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="0956" n="944" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg944"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/12–3044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-30T15:00:00+03:00">December 30,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 30—9:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5060. Molotov has sent me a draft of the additional article referred to in point
                    6 of my 5034, December 27, 9 p.m. It reads as follows: <pb facs="0957" n="945"
                        xml:id="pg945"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Article XIX. The Allied Governments consider the decision of the Vienna
                            Arbitration Commission of November 2, 1938<anchor n="96"
                                xml:id="d875-f1"/> and also the Vienna award of August 30,
                                1940<anchor n="97" xml:id="d875-f2"/> as null and void.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I would appreciate instructions on this point.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
